   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. I did not run it through a parser, so validity rests on my manual check of ring closures and atom counts.\n\n**Fragments, in order around the macrocycle**\n- **Aryl group:** a 2,3,6-trimethoxyphenyl ring, attached through a CH2CH2 chain to the benzylic carbinol carbon.\n- **Carbinol carbon:** the hashed bond to the CH2 gives it the stereo label `[C@H]6` as written. It is esterified by the pipecolic acid carboxyl and bears a meta-substituted phenyl ring.\n- **Pipecolic acid:** an L-type six-membered ring (the wedge goes to the ring CH2). Its nitrogen carries the C(=O)C(=O)C(CH3)2CH2O\u2013C(=O) unit.\n- **Alkene:** the ester carbonyl is attached to CH=CH\u2013CH2\u2013N(CH3). The wavy bond means the geometry is unspecified, so I gave it no / or \\.\n- **Peptide chain:** the N-methylglycine amide runs into Gly (NH\u2013CH2\u2013C=O), then Ser(OtBu), then N-Me-2-naphthylalanine, then norleucine, then N-Me. The N-Me ends in C(=O)CH2\u2013O, which links to the meta position of the phenyl ring.\n- **Stereocentres:** every amino-acid alpha carbon has a wedge in the drawing, and I assigned each from its wedge and neighbour order.\n\nSMILES: COc1ccc(OC)c(CC[C@H]6OC(=O)[C@@H]2CCCCN2C(=O)C(=O)C(C)(C)COC(=O)C=CCN(C)C(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](COC(C)(C)C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCC)N(C)C(=O)COc5cccc6c5)c1OC"
